# Line endings are LF in the repository and LF in the working tree, on every
# platform.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` on a Windows checkout writes CRLF into the
# working tree while the blobs stay LF, so every `git checkout` silently
# rewrites the files it restores. AUDIT_P4 hit exactly that: reverting a
# mutation with `git checkout` flipped four engine files to CRLF, and
# converting them back made `git status` report six modified files with an
# empty content diff. Neither state is wrong and both look like a change, which
# is the worst way for a tree to be clean.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary. Never normalised, never diffed as text.
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
